
====================================================================================================
S1. THE CANONICAL alpha=2 KERNEL AND ITS SPECTRAL MEASURE -- the enabling result
====================================================================================================
  K_2(z) = sqrt(z/(1+z)),  nu = 1/K,  argument z = |a|^2/a0^2 (Theorem B).
  Its cut is where z/(1+z) < 0, i.e. -1 < z < 0. Setting z = -s with 0 < s < 1 gives
  K = i sqrt(s/(1-s)), so Stieltjes inversion yields
      rho(s) = (1/pi) Im K = sqrt(s)*sqrt(1/(1 - s))/pi      on 0 < s < 1   [COMPACT SUPPORT]
  and the Herglotz form must be K_2(z) = 1 - INT_0^1 rho(s) ds/(z+s), because the bare
  resolvent integral vanishes at z -> oo while K_2(oo) = 1.

  sum rule   INT rho/s ds = 1     (must equal K(oo) - K(0) = 1)
  total mass INT rho ds   = 1/2     (finite)
  [OK] the alpha=2 measure satisfies the SAME unit sum rule INT dmu/|t| = 1 that makes a0 additively unrenormalised -- so the property a0's derivation rests on is preserved exactly

           z  K_2 closed form  from the measure    rel err
      0.0001     0.0099995000      0.0099995000   4.16e-15
        0.01     0.0995037190      0.0995037190   5.58e-16
           1     0.7071067812      0.7071067812   0.00e+00
         100     0.9950371902      0.9950371902   0.00e+00
       1e+04     0.9999500037      0.9999500037   0.00e+00
       1e+08     0.9999999950      0.9999999950   0.00e+00
  [OK] the measure reproduces the closed form to 4.2e-15 over eight decades in z -- the representation is verified, not asserted
  [OK] the measure is POSITIVE and the kernel PASSIVE (0 <= K <= 1) -- both premises of the a0 scale derivation hold

  AND IT IS SIMPLER THAN THE PUBLISHED alpha=1 MEASURE, which is worth stating plainly:
  property                     alpha=1 (published)          alpha=2 (the switch)  
  spectral regions             2  (rho_A, rho_B)            1                     
  support                      UNBOUNDED (t -> -inf)        COMPACT  [0,1]        
  additive constant            a = 0.65411                  none                  
  total mass                   DIVERGENT                    1/2                   
  sum rule INT dmu/|t|         1                            1                     
  branch point                 t = -1/4                     t = -1                
  The UNBOUNDED support of the alpha=1 measure is what produced BOTH the exact law and the
  1/(2x) planetary tail -- its divergent total mass is exactly the 1/x rather than 1/x^2
  approach to the passivity bound. The switch removes the divergence and the tail together.

====================================================================================================
S2. TRIAGE -- what moves and what does not, computed
====================================================================================================
  Both kernels share the DEEP limit (K ~ sqrt z), so deep-regime results are invariant.
  They differ in the TRANSITION and HIGH regimes. Checking each banked class:

  (a) DEEP REGIME -- BTFR / cluster-scale y. nu ratio alpha2/alpha1:
   y = g_bar/a0  nu alpha=1  nu alpha=2    ratio
         0.0001    100.0050    100.0025   1.0000
          0.001     31.6386     31.6307   0.9998
           0.01     10.0499     10.0250   0.9975
          0.037      5.2941      5.2471   0.9911
            0.1      3.3166      3.2423   0.9776
  [OK] in the deep regime the two kernels agree to 2.2% or better, so BTFR, the deep-MOND slope 1/2, and cluster eta (median y = 0.037) are NEAR-INVARIANT -- those banked numbers do not need re-deriving, only re-checking

  (b) TRANSITION REGIME -- the RAR and the wide-binary EFE, y ~ 1-3:
              y  nu alpha=1  nu alpha=2    ratio
            0.5      1.7321      1.6005   0.9240
              1      1.4142      1.2720   0.8995
            1.9      1.2354      1.1072   0.8962
              3      1.1547      1.0492   0.9087
      committed SPARC fit: alpha=1 0.1083 dex, alpha=2 0.1116 dex, cost +0.0033 (0.10 sigma_int)

  (c) HIGH REGIME -- the planets. This is the whole point of the switch:
  footing             anomaly alpha=1   vs bound  anomaly alpha=2   vs bound
  canonical rho_DE         4.6800e-11      1279x       1.3167e-18  3.60e-05x
  alt rho_total            5.6500e-11      1544x       1.3167e-18  3.60e-05x
  [OK] the switch takes the Earth anomaly from ABOVE the 2-sigma bound to BELOW it on both footings -- the liability the switch was adopted for is discharged

  (d) THE EXACT LAW -- withdrawn, and this is the price:
      alpha=1: g_obs^2 - g_bar^2 - a0 g_bar = 0  (identically zero)
      alpha=2: g_bar = g_obs^2/sqrt(g_obs^2 + a0^2), a QUARTIC in g_obs -- no exact
      algebraic relation of the banked form exists. The 'a0-line' identity is WITHDRAWN.
  [OK] the exact relation is an alpha=1 identity and does not survive -- so every statement of it in the corpus is now a HISTORICAL claim, not a live one

