S5. WHAT A COMPLETE MIGRATION REQUIRES -- scoped, not hand-waved
====================================================================================================
  Blast radius measured by grep: 314 scripts reference the alpha=1 kernel or the exact law,
  267 of them in real_research/, prep_2026/ and opus_48_extended_research/.
  A blind substitution is NOT the migration, because those scripts' internal checks assert
  their own printed values; flipping the kernel would make them fail, and 'fixing' the
  thresholds to match would destroy the audit trail that makes the corpus self-verifying.
  The order that actually works, in dependency order:
   1. DONE HERE: the alpha=2 kernel + its verified spectral measure (S1). Nothing downstream
      can migrate without this.
   2. DONE HERE: triage (S2) -- deep-regime results are near-invariant and need only
      re-checking; transition/high-regime results need genuine re-derivation.
   3. OWED NOW, time-boxed: the DR4 pre-registration amendment (S3), before ~Dec 2026.
   4. OWNER'S CALL: erratum scope for the published DOIs (S4).
   5. THEN the script sweep, done as re-derivations with their numbers RECOMPUTED and their
      old values retained as superseded -- not as a find-and-replace. Highest value first:
      rar_framework_a0_mlfit, clusters_eta_audit, the wide-binary pre-reg chain, the forest
      set (already kernel-argument-corrected today), the growth chain.
   6. LAST: the covariant sector, which needs the loop results re-run on the new measure.
  ESTIMATE, stated so it can be argued with: steps 3-4 are days; step 5 is the bulk; step 6
  is a research project, not an edit.
  [OK] migration scoped in dependency order with the unsafe shortcut named

====================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  THE SWITCH IS APPLIED WHERE IT CAN BE APPLIED CORRECTLY TODAY:
   * The alpha=2 kernel has a verified positive spectral measure with the SAME unit sum rule,
     so a0 = cH_Lambda/Z survives the switch intact -- and the measure is strictly simpler
     than the published one (single region, compact support, finite mass, no constant).
   * The planetary liability is DISCHARGED on both footings.
   * Deep-regime results (BTFR, cluster eta, the 1/2 slope) are near-invariant.
   * The RAR costs +0.0033 dex, 0.10 sigma_int.
   * The EXACT LAW is withdrawn. That is the price and it is the only one.
  WHAT IS NOT DONE, AND MUST NOT BE PRETENDED DONE:
   * 267 scripts still compute on the alpha=1 kernel. Their numbers are now labelled
     alpha=1 results, not framework results, until re-derived.
   * The DR4 pre-registration amendment is OWED and time-boxed.
   * The published DOIs state a law the framework no longer holds. Erratum scope is the
     owner's decision.
   * The covariant/loop sector is still on the old measure.
  [OK] verdict separates what was migrated from what was only scoped
